\f1\b Module 2\'97 venv, pip, requirements.txt, and Git hygiene with .gitignore
\f0\b0 \
Let's map this to something you already know from Xcode, since the concept is identical even though the tooling looks different.\

\f1\b The Swift/Xcode Analogy First
\f0\b0 \
In Xcode, when you create a project, it automatically manages dependencies via 
\f1\b Swift Package Manager
\f0\b0  or 
\f1\b CocoaPods
\f0\b0  \'97 each project gets its own isolated set of libraries, so Project A using Alamofire 5.0 doesn't conflict with Project B using Alamofire 4.0.\
Python has no Xcode to do this invisibly for you. You have to set it up yourself using 
\f1\b virtual environments (venv)
\f0\b0 . Skipping this step is the #1 reason beginners' Python projects break mysteriously.\

\f1\b The Problem venv Solves
\f0\b0 \
Without a virtual environment, every Python package you install goes into one 
\f1\b global
\f0\b0  location on your Mac. This means:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Project A needs requests==2.28\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Project B needs requests==2.31\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Installing one breaks the other\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Sound familiar? It's exactly the "dependency hell" problem CocoaPods/SPM solve for you automatically \'97 Python just makes you do it manually.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Core Concept: venv = "a private Python install per project"
\f0\b0 \
A virtual environment is a self-contained folder with its own Python interpreter and its own package library, isolated from your system Python and from other projects.\

\f1\b Setting One Up
