try:\
\'a0 \'a0 risky_code()\
except Exception as e:\
\'a0 \'a0 print(f"Something went wrong: \{e\}")\
as e captures the actual error object, so you can inspect or print its message. This is like Swift's catch let error capturing the error instance.\
