\f1\b 1. Basic try/except
\f0\b0  Write a function safe_divide(a, b) that divides a by b, but catches ZeroDivisionError and returns/prints a friendly message instead of crashing. Test it with safe_divide(10, 0) and safe_divide(10, 2).\

\f1\b 2. Multiple except blocks
\f0\b0  Write a function that takes user input (as a string) and tries to convert it to an integer using int(). Catch ValueError if the input isn't a valid number, and print an appropriate message either way.\

\f1\b 3. Custom raise
\f0\b0  Update your classify_experience(years) function from Module 1 to raise ValueError("Years cannot be negative") if years < 0. Wrap a call to it in a try/except and test with classify_experience(-3).\

