\f1\b Module 1: NumPy essentials \'97 arrays, vectorized ops
\f0\b0 \
Let's dive into NumPy \'97 this is where Python starts feeling less like general-purpose scripting and more like the actual tooling used in AI/ML work. NumPy is a 
\f1\b library
\f0\b0  for numerical computing, and considered a foundational piece of Python's scientific computing / AI ecosystem.\

\f1\b Why NumPy Exists
\f0\b0 \
Regular Python lists are flexible but slow for numerical work, and they don't support math operations the way you'd want. NumPy introduces the 
\f1\b array
\f0\b0  \'97 a fixed-type, high-performance data structure built for numerical computation. Nearly every AI/ML library (PyTorch, TensorFlow, pandas, scikit-learn) is built on top of NumPy arrays under the hood.\

